{"uuid":"ecf77f27-df0f-47c4-99c2-48d7fa46a137","variant":"base","mode":"judged","scenario":"judged.mjs step 0","viewport":"desktop","viewports":["1440x900"],"verdict":"pass","notes":"First real card with a void activation. With Revenant Automaton and Aspiring Guardian in the player's void and two back-rank characters, only the player's void pile carries data-pile-selection=playable (green ring); pressing it opens the void browser where the Automaton tile is a ringed button and the Guardian tile is a plain non-pressable tile. Pressing the Automaton tile closes the browser and opens 'Abandon a character / From Revenant Automaton' with Cancel, offering exactly the two back-rank characters (no board ring on the candidates, the same presentation the hv-umm2.490 fixture showed); tapping one materializes the Automaton into the back rank from the void, its own Materialized trigger gains 1 point (score 0 -> 1, shown 1/25), the abandoned character goes to the void and the pile ring clears. One abilityActivated event (ability 1, source the void instance). Battle log reads abandoned / activated / entered play / triggered ability resolved / gained 1 point in plain language. No horizontal overflow; window.__caps empty after each step.","bead":"hv-umm2.151","commit":"7c3877a8a4b54edf8358225e689bee135811a028","screens":["invocations/run-SCTexR/revenant-void-ringed-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/revenant-void-browser-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/revenant-abandon-prompt-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/revenant-resolved-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/revenant-log-desktop.png"],"caps":[]}
{"uuid":"ed4d5342-0690-40b7-ab48-6b76035466f2","variant":"base","mode":"judged","scenario":"judged.mjs steps 1-2","viewport":"desktop","viewports":["1440x900"],"verdict":"pass","notes":"D21 sample. As player: tapping the ready Chaos Crasher opens 'Choose an ability' listing both abilities by printed cost and effect plus Cancel; the erode ability exhausts it, auto-discards the one hand card and erodes the top 2 deck cards into the void (deck -2), log 'You discarded ... / ... was eroded into your void' x2. The exhausted Crasher stays ringed for its 4-energy ability, and a tap goes straight to 'Choose a target 0/1 selected' over the void characters only (the Crasher, still in play, is not offered: targets are chosen before costs, rules section Targeting); the self-abandon cost auto-answers with a 'Chosen for You' notice, 4 energy is paid, the Crasher goes to the void and the chosen void character returns to hand. As enemy: the scripted enemy activation abandons its Crasher and returns Marked Direwolf from its void to its hand; the human's log reads 'Your opponent abandoned Chaos Crasher ... activated Chaos Crasher ... Marked Direwolf returned to your opponent's hand.' No horizontal overflow; window.__caps empty after each step. A tap on the Crasher made while the erode's card-travel presentation is still playing does nothing; the same tap after it settles activates.","bead":"hv-umm2.151","commit":"7c3877a8a4b54edf8358225e689bee135811a028","screens":["invocations/run-SCTexR/crasher-chooser-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/crasher-eroded-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/crasher-return-target-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/crasher-returned-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/crasher-log-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/crasher-enemy-resolved-desktop.png","invocations/run-SCTexR/crasher-enemy-log-desktop.png"],"caps":[]}
